  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c1878eb0-df1a-5e65-9254-faad0dadbc19" activityNameId="2ec9a74b-767d-51f4-ac8b-6dae68e2c039" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sulfidic tailings, off-site</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sulfidic tailings, off-site
na;
Synonyms: Flotationsschlämme; 
UUID: ff7d71b2-b5be-40d1-a1b7-92dcdbfe6663
Waste-specific short- and long-term emissions to ground water from tailings impoundment leachate. Land transformation and occupation.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Mechanically stable tailings impoundment. Spontaneous renaturation after closure.
Time period: Average waste composition from literature references. Transfer coefficients from prospective, tailings-specific model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Tailings model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from large literature survey. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions during a generic ecological planning horizon (60'000a). Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ff7d71b2-b5be-40d1-a1b7-92dcdbfe6663.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
